e\n   CPU throughout). Within shared-machine noise; measured, not asserted.\n4. **Zero red errors**: none in the session beyond 1.5's deliberate\n   selftest-induced text (filtered by exact string, 0 remaining).\n\n\nNon-pausing windows do not halt (forcePause IS the predicate that kills the\nletter queue, not a proxy); no suppression flag ships (there is no honest\n\"plough on\" — a suppressed halt means the letter queue is switched off, and a\nfuture caller who wants it wants 3.5's routing); dismissal stays a dev-gated\nfixture step (`dialogs-clear`) where no player verb can reach it.\n\n\nOnce an advance halts with `dialog`, no shipped verb clears the stack —\nevery later advance halts at 0 ticks until a human intervenes. Strictly\nbetter than silent letter-queue corruption (a stuck run is visible), but a\nten-day unattended run cannot survive its first timed letter without 3.5's\ndialog routing. Amended on 3.5 and 4.3.\n\nAlso worth knowing (worker finding, decompile-verified): the dev debug menu\n(Dialog_Debug family) sets forcePause, so opening it on a watched bench WILL\nhalt the next advance with reason \"dialog\". Correct, and will surprise\nsomeone once.","files":null}]}